Reference quirk: `<list>` is not an element of the schema this parser targets.

usfm-grammar renders the USFM 3.2 `\list-s\*` … `\list-e\*` pair as a `<list>`
element wrapping the list paragraphs, and drops the milestones themselves.
tcdocs' `grammar/usx.rnc` has no `<list>` element: its `List` production (line
752) is a plain `element para` with a list style, and `\list-s` is not among
the `Para.para.style.enum` values either. An unrecognised milestone is written
as `<ms>` — tcdocs' own reference files do that for `zaln-s`, `zaln-e`, `ts-s`
and `zms`, none of which is in `Milestone.style.enum` — so this moves the two
milestones back into the paragraphs they were written in and flattens the
wrapper away. The list paragraphs themselves are unchanged.

--- origin.xml
+++ origin.xml
@@ -24,19 +24,17 @@
   <chapter eid="GEN 2"/>
   <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="GEN 3"/>
   <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="GEN 3:1"/>Now the newly introduced list markers
+<ms style="list-s"/></para>
+  <para style="lh">optional list header
 </para>
-  <list>
-    <para style="lh">optional list header
+  <para style="li1">list entry 1
 </para>
-    <para style="li1">list entry 1
+  <para style="li1">list entry 2
 </para>
-    <para style="li1">list entry 2
+  <para style="li3">list entry 3
 </para>
-    <para style="li3">list entry 3
-</para>
-    <para style="lf">optional list footer
-<verse eid="GEN 3:1"/></para>
-  </list>
+  <para style="lf">optional list footer
+<ms style="list-e"/><verse eid="GEN 3:1"/></para>
   <para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="GEN 3:2"/>This was introduced in 3.2 version of usfm spec.<verse eid="GEN 3:2"/></para>
   <chapter eid="GEN 3"/>
 </usx>
